WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.411
October 1958.

00:00:01.421 --> 00:00:04.899
A science lab's open day, and there's

00:00:04.909 --> 00:00:05.683
a line.

00:00:05.829 --> 00:00:09.381
Physicist William Higinbotham
thought science exhibits were

00:00:09.391 --> 00:00:11.903
dull, so he built a game.

00:00:11.913 --> 00:00:14.640
The screen is an oscilloscope, just five

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:15.995
inches across.

00:00:16.005 --> 00:00:18.030
The ball is a dot of light.

00:00:18.043 --> 00:00:19.945
Turn the dial to aim, press the

00:00:19.955 --> 00:00:21.145
button to hit.

00:00:21.155 --> 00:00:23.370
It's tennis, seen from the side.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.378
It's called Tennis for Two.

00:00:25.388 --> 00:00:27.993
Hundreds of visitors line up to play.

00:00:28.003 --> 00:00:30.043
The next year, you could even play

00:00:30.053 --> 00:00:31.855
it with the gravity of the Moon,

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:32.989
or Jupiter.

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:35.122
It's one of the earliest video games

00:00:35.132 --> 00:00:36.307
ever made.
